      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{63691297469f06772579fe6f|full_name}: >>Would myou ind clarifying your issue, or providing reproduction steps?\n\n  Click on \"auto fix\" button on VRCSDK control pannel.\n\n  Expected Behavior : VRCSDK fix audio problem.\n\n  Actual Behavior : Audio range changed to too short.\n\n>>Would a confirmation prompt help? \n\n  If it warned that \"auto fix\" will change audio range, I think so.\n\n>>Or the Use AudioSource Volume Curve option?\n\n  It works. But why doesn't  VRCSDK use this option when \"auto fix\"?\n\n  Important point is that AudioSource is not necessarily to use \"spatial audio source\". Skilled developper knows that, but beginner does not. \n\n  The some prefabs which selled on booth is not using \"spatial audio source\". If someone use such prefab, \"auto fix\" button popups on VRCSDK control pannel, and it is \"auto break\" button on this situation.\n\n  I faced \"spatial audio source\" problem when mentoring a begginer.\n\n  \"spatial audio source\" isn't supporting Multi-object editting, so I recommended them delete all that component from hundreds of GameObject.\n\n  They got confusing because SDK and mentor say different things.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
